.TH UNITDECK-TUI 1 "2026" "UnitDeck" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unitdeck-tui \- manage systemd system and user services from a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unitdeck-tui
.RI [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The terminal interface of UnitDeck, in the spirit of htop: two tabs (system and user
services), search, state filter and single-key actions shown in the footer: start, stop,
restart, enable/disable, mask/unmask, logs, edit with drop-ins, new service from a template,
restore original, delete, reset failed state, linger, daemon-reload.
.PP
It never runs as root. In a graphical session polkit shows the desktop dialog; on a TTY or
over SSH the screen is handed to
.BR pkttyagent (1),
which asks for the password in the terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unitdeck (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Nicola Palmieri (n1c0p), https://github.com/n1c0p/UnitDeck
